S(10,1,r'Consider the update equation for SMDP Q-learning:'+'\n'+r'$Q(s,a)=Q(s,a)+\alpha[A+B\max_{a^\prime}Q(s^\prime,a^\prime)-Q(s,a)]$'+'\nWhich of the following are the correct values of A and B?\n'+r'($r_k$ is the reward received at time step $k$, and $\gamma$ is the discount factor)',r'$A=r_t;\ B=\gamma$||$A=r_t+\gamma r_{t+1}+\ldots+\gamma^{\tau-1}r_{t+\tau};\ B=\gamma^\tau$||$A=\gamma^t r_t+\gamma^{t+1}r_{t+1}+\ldots+\gamma^{t+\tau-1}r_{t+\tau};\ B=\gamma^{t+\tau}$||$A=\gamma^{t-1}r_{t+\tau};\ B=\gamma^t$')
S(10,2,r'Consider a SMDP in which the next state and the reward only depend on the previous state and action i.e. $P(s^\prime,\tau\mid s,a)=P(s^\prime\mid s,a)P(\tau\mid s,a)$, $R(s,a,\tau,s^\prime)=R(s,a,s^\prime)$. If we solve the above SMDP with conventional Q-learning we will end up with the same policy as solving it with SMDP Q-learning.',r'yes, because now $\tau$ won’t change anything and we end up with same states and action sequences||no, because $\tau$ still depends on the state, action pair and discounting may have an effect on the final policies.||no, because the next state will still depend on the $\tau$.||yes, because the bellman equation is same for both methods in this case.')
S(10,5,options='Statement1 is True and Statement2 is True.||Statement1 is True and Statement2 is False.||Statement1 is False and Statement2 is True.||Statement1 is False and Statement2 is False.')
S(10,7,r'In SMDP, consider the case when $\tau$ is fixed for all state, action pairs. Will we always get the same policy for conventional Q-learning and SMDP Q learning then? Provide answer for the three cases when $\tau=3,\tau=2,\tau=1$.','yes, yes, no||no, no, no||yes, yes, yes||no, no, yes')
S(10,9,r'Suppose that we model a robot in a room as an SMDP, such that the position of the robot in the room is the state of the SMDP. Which of the following scenarios satisfy the assumption that the next state and transition time are independent of each other given the current state and action i.e. $P(s^\prime,\tau\mid s,a)=P(s^\prime\mid s,a)P(\tau\mid s,a)$? (Assume that primitive actions – <left, right, up, down> take a single time step to execute.)')
S(10,10,r'Which of the following is a correct Bellman equation for an SMDP?'+'\n'+r'Note: $R(s,a,s^\prime)\Rightarrow$ reward is a function of only $s,a$ and $s^\prime$.',r'$V^*(s)=\max_{a\in A(s)}[R(s,a,\tau,s^\prime)+\gamma^\tau P(s^\prime\mid s,a)V^*(s^\prime)]$||$V^*(s)=\max_{a\in A(s)}[\sum_{s^\prime,\tau}P(s^\prime\mid s,a,\tau)(R(s,a,\tau,s^\prime)+\gamma V^*(s^\prime))]$||$V^*(s)=\max_{a\in A(s)}[\sum_{s^\prime,\tau}P(s^\prime,\tau\mid s,a)(R(s,a,\tau,s^\prime)+\gamma^\tau V^*(s^\prime))]$||$V^*(s)=\max_{a\in A(s)}[\sum_{s^\prime,\tau}P(s^\prime,\tau\mid s,a)(R(s,a,s^\prime)+\gamma V^*(s^\prime))]$')
